{"title":"2023 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 10","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Coordinate_Geometry)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Coordinate Geometry)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Polar_Coordinates)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Polar Coordinates)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_1_by_OmegaLearn\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 1 by OmegaLearn</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/7/3f79c3676b62fb47243e0d357c87115b6f3395e4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$xy$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"22\" height=\"13\" />-plane, a circle of radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> with center on the positive <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />-axis is tangent to the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />-axis at the origin, and a circle with radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> with center on the positive <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />-axis is tangent to the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />-axis at the origin. What is the slope of the line passing through the two points at which these circles intersect?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/b/2cb73561306b9437481cdb15597b1a865060d2d5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ \\dfrac{2}{7} \\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ \\dfrac{3}{7}  \\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ \\dfrac{2}{\\sqrt{29}}  \\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ \\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt{29}}  \\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ \\dfrac{2}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"419\" height=\"43\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The center of the first circle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/6/b86f58cb609fa753024f1173510c877971f8e4e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(4,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />.\nThe center of the second circle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/7/0c73c07f74df46221dd0273f44b001fef277e9fc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0,10)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"47\" height=\"18\" />.\nThus, the slope of the line that passes through these two centers is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/a/fbaed0c7a1457456a2e03b6bfb589df141482161.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$- \\frac{10}{4} = - \\frac{5}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"90\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>Because this line is the perpendicular bisector of the line that passes through two intersecting points of two circles, the slope of the latter line is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/5/5256a318cc0048fe633ea63682a59ca815c30a48.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{-1}{- \\frac{5}{2}} = \\boxed{\\textbf{(E) } \\frac{2}{5}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"113\" height=\"50\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n~Steven Chen (Professor Chen Education Palace, www.professorchenedu.com)\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Coordinate_Geometry.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Coordinate_Geometry)\">Solution 2 (Coordinate Geometry)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Coordinate Geometry)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The first circle can be written as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/c/19c5ab77c8bf2fc30f5ed79ac0a3fee954936a01.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x-4)^2 + y^2 = 4^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"145\" height=\"21\" /> we'll call this equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/9/0d9c3b1c142cbd3f8217dabc160c57e4750df241.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" />\nThe second can we writen as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/9/ff9f3219a263e7891bce3453c587f1ea52da552b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2 + (y-10)^2 = 10^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"163\" height=\"21\" />, we'll call this equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/f/62f62a19f0425d8e6121ca0c1cfd3ce96e43c9c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Expanding <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/9/0d9c3b1c142cbd3f8217dabc160c57e4750df241.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" />:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/d/ccd91f56d5206b93fa85e4eb5c3992185a426614.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} x^2 -8x + 4^2 + y^2 &amp;= 4^2 \\\\ x^2 - 8x + y^2 &amp;= 0 \\end{align*}\" width=\"176\" height=\"46\" />\nExapnding <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/f/62f62a19f0425d8e6121ca0c1cfd3ce96e43c9c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/8/278349eec2120b1091d0e8b1dcd429221da97da8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} x^2 + y^2 -20y + 10^2 = 10^2\\\\ x^2 + y^2 - 20y = 0 \\end{align*}\" width=\"203\" height=\"46\" />\n</p><p>Now we can set the equations equal to eachother:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/6/9c623ccb710901028ec63bb78a7077bc7216fec9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} x^2 - 8x + y^2 &amp;= x^2 + y^2 - 20y \\\\ \\frac{8}{20}x &amp;= y \\\\ \\frac{2}{5}x &amp;= y \\end{align*}\" width=\"228\" height=\"108\" />\nThis is in slope intercept form therefore the slope is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/6/516478a3e2b5d9dc6859b4eb403ea3c1192ea0fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E) } \\frac{2}{5}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"60\" height=\"49\" />.\n</p>\n<figure class=\"mw-halign-center\" typeof=\"mw:File/Thumb\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:Amc12B_2023_P10.PNG\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/2/2e/Amc12B_2023_P10.PNG/600px-Amc12B_2023_P10.PNG\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"600\" height=\"496\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/2/2e/Amc12B_2023_P10.PNG/900px-Amc12B_2023_P10.PNG 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/2/2e/Amc12B_2023_P10.PNG 2x\" /></a><figcaption></figcaption></figure> \n<p>~<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php/User:Cyantist\">luckuso</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Polar_Coordinates.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Polar_Coordinates)\">Solution 3 (Polar Coordinates)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Polar Coordinates)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In polar coordinates, a circle of radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> tangent to the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />-axis with center on the positive <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />-axis has equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/4/48496401d26f2b07d2f93dcc2455414a853ef091.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r = 2a\\cos\\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"93\" height=\"14\" />, and a circle tangent to the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />-axis with center on the positive <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />-axis has equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/7/e57ed2b6ccf75b38efb76410b5bb1aec28e9df25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r = 2b\\sin\\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"89\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>The first circle (radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, center <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/6/b86f58cb609fa753024f1173510c877971f8e4e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(4,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />) has polar equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/7/627ed5ad659617be512616859f9e2862d7c5e6f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r = 8\\cos\\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"83\" height=\"14\" />, and the second circle (radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, center <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/7/0c73c07f74df46221dd0273f44b001fef277e9fc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0,10)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"47\" height=\"18\" />) has polar equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/0/2701e69097b231d01b9982a85d7aef5737e8f287.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r = 20\\sin\\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"90\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>The origin lies on both circles, so it is one intersection point. Setting the equations equal for the other:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/6/766b4879c4856446e0944246236028c8054b7a34.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[8\\cos\\theta = 20\\sin\\theta \\implies \\tan\\theta = \\frac{8}{20} = \\frac{2}{5}\\]\" width=\"298\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/f/69f5ff57a3118c779a81ae09ff24e5a3b9bfe2d8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan\\theta = \\frac{y}{x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"79\" height=\"34\" />, both intersection points (the origin and the point at angle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/e/52e8ed7a3ba22130ad3984eb2cd413406475a689.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />) lie on the line through the origin with slope <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/3/3e3230e11561a7290dc4774c65dcff5e3ccd03f0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan\\theta$\" width=\"38\" height=\"13\" />. Therefore, the slope of the line through the two intersection points is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/4/aa44c95f21652a9be880b68f54bdb99690da8405.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\dfrac{2}{5}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"26\" height=\"49\" />.\n</p><p>~<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external autonumber\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php/User:Literal\">[1]</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_1_by_OmegaLearn\">Video Solution 1 by OmegaLearn</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 1 by OmegaLearn\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/IUB6r1iNgpU\">https://youtu.be/IUB6r1iNgpU</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/sjJMWtL_CEY\">https://youtu.be/sjJMWtL_CEY</a>\n</p><p>~Steven Chen (Professor Chen Education Palace, www.professorchenedu.com)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12B\" title=\"2023 AMC 12B\">2023 AMC 12B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12B_Problems\" title=\"2023 AMC 12B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2023 AMC 12B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/co